selenium-webdriver-at-spi.py: do not trust a cached missing Component

libatspi can keep a negative interface list across Qt visibility changes.
In a real Fedora 44 session, a public WebDriver rect read while the preview
popup was hidden made later rect reads and element-origin pointer moves
fail with NotImplementedError even while the popup was visibly open.
Clearing that object's cache allowed the same rect request to succeed.
The Fedora 44 requests reproduce the cache defect. The first cache lookup
in the original native CI run was not captured.

Before the element rect and an element pointer origin in POST /actions
read the Component, clear that object's cache (clear_cache_single, since
at-spi2-core 2.50) only when get_component_iface() says it has none. A
cached Component is kept: its getPosition()/getSize() already call the live
object, and a hidden Qt popup returns 0x0 through it while a fresh
interface list would lack Component. Clearing it would turn that 0x0 rect
into an error. No geometry request is replayed and no exception is caught.
If the refreshed lookup still lacks Component, it raises as before.

--- a/selenium-webdriver-at-spi.py
+++ b/selenium-webdriver-at-spi.py
@@ -702,6 +702,8 @@
 def session_element_rect(session_id, element_id):
     session = sessions[session_id]
     element = session.elements[element_id]
+    if element.get_component_iface() is None:
+        element.clear_cache_single()
     x, y = element.queryComponent().getPosition(pyatspi.XY_SCREEN)
     w, h = element.queryComponent().getSize()
     return json.dumps({'value': {'x': x, 'y': y, 'width': w, 'height': h} }), 200, {'content-type': 'application/json'}
@@ -981,6 +983,8 @@
                 element_id = next(iter(action["origin"].values()))
                 action["origin"] = "viewport"
                 element = session.elements[element_id]
+                if element.get_component_iface() is None:
+                    element.clear_cache_single()
                 x, y = element.queryComponent().getPosition(pyatspi.XY_SCREEN)
                 action["x"] += x
                 action["y"] += y
